  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degree incidence. Initialize thicknesses using quarter-wave optical thickness at 550nm (TiO2 approximately 57nm, SiO2 approximately 96nm physical thickness). Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with bounds [20, 180] nm per layer. Evaluate performance for both s and p polarizations across 450-650nm (target high reflectance) and 700-1000nm (target high transmittance). Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating TiO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
